WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:01.204
- We're having Native American food.

00:00:01.204 --> 00:00:02.408
- Which is really, we're just eating

00:00:02.408 --> 00:00:04.008
American food, for the first time.

00:00:04.008 --> 00:00:06.548
(upbeat funky music)

00:00:06.548 --> 00:00:08.068
It smells amazing in here!

00:00:09.918 --> 00:00:10.988
- Ohh.

00:00:10.988 --> 00:00:12.687
- I am so excited to see how people react

00:00:12.687 --> 00:00:14.048
to this. (laughs)

00:00:14.048 --> 00:00:15.248
They're probably going to die.

00:00:15.248 --> 00:00:18.408
(dramatic upbeat music)

00:00:18.408 --> 00:00:19.567
- I ate a light lunch today actually

00:00:19.567 --> 00:00:20.928
to prepare for this.

00:00:20.928 --> 00:00:21.648
And that's why.

00:00:21.648 --> 00:00:22.588
- We have to share?

00:00:22.588 --> 00:00:24.508
(both make airplane sounds)

00:00:26.008 --> 00:00:27.868
- Oh my God, it smells so nutty.

00:00:27.868 --> 00:00:29.408
- This taste healthy as (beep).

00:00:29.408 --> 00:00:30.408
- I feel like this is what you eat

00:00:30.408 --> 00:00:31.428
when you have your life together.

00:00:31.428 --> 00:00:32.648
- So many grains.
- [Guy] Grains.

00:00:32.648 --> 00:00:33.427
A lot of grains.

00:00:33.427 --> 00:00:35.588
- My poop is gonna just be perfect.

00:00:35.588 --> 00:00:37.608
- This is definitely like
a unique kind of rice.

00:00:37.608 --> 00:00:38.748
I don't think I've ever
had anything like this.

00:00:38.748 --> 00:00:40.128
- What point in history do you think

00:00:40.128 --> 00:00:42.018
we started pooping so poorly?

00:00:42.018 --> 00:00:43.788
- Hmm, whenever white people
got involved. (laughter)

00:00:43.788 --> 00:00:45.558
- Wild rice, is not actually rice.

00:00:45.558 --> 00:00:47.538
It's a grass seed.

00:00:47.538 --> 00:00:48.288
- It's not really rice.

00:00:48.288 --> 00:00:49.778
- We just ate grass?

00:00:49.778 --> 00:00:50.208
- Oh.

00:00:50.208 --> 00:00:52.127
- Well, we learn something everyday.

00:00:52.127 --> 00:00:55.428
(upbeat music)

00:00:55.428 --> 00:00:57.758
- We got ourselves some.
- [Guy] Oh, this smells good!

00:00:57.758 --> 00:00:59.568
- This is like soup my grandma would make.

00:00:59.568 --> 00:01:00.328
- There's corn.

00:01:00.328 --> 00:01:01.088
There's beans.

00:01:01.088 --> 00:01:02.128
There's a bunch of different vegetables.

00:01:02.128 --> 00:01:04.748
- The three sisters are
beans, corn, and squash

00:01:04.748 --> 00:01:06.728
and they were all grown together,

00:01:06.728 --> 00:01:08.548
almost like one big crop.

00:01:08.548 --> 00:01:10.608
- Fourth sister, she
can go (beep) herself.

00:01:10.608 --> 00:01:11.948
- The cornstalk would grow.

00:01:11.948 --> 00:01:13.585
The bean sprout would
grow up the cornstalk.

00:01:13.585 --> 00:01:15.424
The squash would cover the ground

00:01:15.424 --> 00:01:16.305
and protect the root system.

00:01:16.305 --> 00:01:17.365
- Oh...
- [Guy] They're called the

00:01:17.365 --> 00:01:18.565
three sisters because they lived together.

00:01:18.565 --> 00:01:20.225
- Oh, that's so sweet.
- [Guy] Wow.

00:01:20.225 --> 00:01:21.625
- I want to hang out with those sisters

00:01:21.625 --> 00:01:23.012
because this (beep) is good!

00:01:23.012 --> 00:01:24.302
- Definitely see the similarities between

00:01:24.302 --> 00:01:25.141
Native American food

00:01:25.141 --> 00:01:26.462
and African American food.

00:01:26.462 --> 00:01:27.642
- This definitely tastes
like something that

00:01:27.642 --> 00:01:28.622
latin folk would make.

00:01:28.622 --> 00:01:30.242
- It actually tastes like
tortilla soup a little bit too.

00:01:30.242 --> 00:01:31.722
- It feels familiar to me.

00:01:31.722 --> 00:01:32.562
It feels like home.

00:01:32.562 --> 00:01:36.482
(upbeat fast-paced music)

00:01:36.482 --> 00:01:38.241
- I've been waiting all day for this.

00:01:38.241 --> 00:01:39.842
- Oohhh.
- [Guy] Wow!

00:01:39.842 --> 00:01:40.962
- It's cute!

00:01:40.962 --> 00:01:42.802
- Aww man, this is just
a frisbee of goodness,

00:01:42.802 --> 00:01:43.562
right here.

00:01:43.562 --> 00:01:44.842
- I should, I'm just gonna pick it up.

00:01:44.842 --> 00:01:46.791
- Mmm, (beep)!

00:01:46.791 --> 00:01:47.442
- This is so good.

00:01:47.442 --> 00:01:51.272
- An Indian taco is fry bread with chili

00:01:51.272 --> 00:01:53.812
and all this dank ass stuff. (laughs)

00:01:53.812 --> 00:01:55.272
- This one is not healthy.

00:01:55.272 --> 00:01:56.802
- This is diabetes on a plate.

00:01:56.802 --> 00:01:59.261
- Dang, this is some good
ass drunk food right here.

00:01:59.261 --> 00:02:00.203
- Oh my God!

00:02:00.203 --> 00:02:01.982
- This bread taste different
than any kind of other

00:02:01.982 --> 00:02:02.541
bread I've ever had.

00:02:02.541 --> 00:02:03.682
- And it kicks a funnel cake's ass.

00:02:03.682 --> 00:02:06.301
- I feel like a lot of
Native culture hasn't crossed

00:02:06.301 --> 00:02:08.502
over into main true American culture

00:02:08.502 --> 00:02:09.742
and that's a damn shame

00:02:09.742 --> 00:02:12.002
because this food is so damn good.

00:02:12.002 --> 00:02:14.522
- There's certain cultures
in which we don't have

00:02:14.522 --> 00:02:15.342
access to.

00:02:15.342 --> 00:02:17.042
I mean, I don't know
why we don't have a ton

00:02:17.042 --> 00:02:18.362
of access to Native American culture.

00:02:18.362 --> 00:02:19.742
- I feel like people think that like

00:02:19.742 --> 00:02:21.562
all Native traditions and everything

00:02:21.562 --> 00:02:23.902
is like dead and this is some ancient food

00:02:23.902 --> 00:02:26.762
that we are reincarnating, right now.

00:02:26.762 --> 00:02:29.042
It's still something that
people eat every single day.

00:02:29.042 --> 00:02:31.422
- And if this is hiding
within Native culture,

00:02:31.422 --> 00:02:33.402
then I can't imagine what
else is waiting for us.

00:02:33.402 --> 00:02:34.701
- It's a shame because obviously

00:02:34.701 --> 00:02:36.942
Native American culture
has so much to offer.

00:02:36.942 --> 00:02:38.321
And food is just one of them.

00:02:38.321 --> 00:02:39.641
- I'm honored to be eating this.

00:02:39.641 --> 00:02:40.762
This deliciousness.

00:02:40.762 --> 00:02:42.098
- It's so good.

00:02:42.098 --> 00:02:44.628
What, what do you want from me?

